    "faq": [
        {
            "question": "What is the difference between AG Grid and MUI DataGrid?",
            "answer": "MUI DataGrid is the free component of MUI X Data Grid. Both grids render a complete UI and have a free, MIT-licensed version. AG Grid supports React, Angular, Vue and plain JavaScript; MUI X Data Grid is built for React only and depends on Material UI. In the free MUI X Data Grid, row virtualisation is limited to 100 rows, and column pinning and multi-column sorting need the Pro plan; AG Grid Community includes all three. Row grouping, pivoting and Excel export are paid features in both."
        },
        {
            "question": "Is MUI Data Grid Pro free?",
            "answer": "No. MUI X Data Grid has a free, MIT-licensed Community version, but Pro is a paid plan: $299 per developer per year, or $657 per developer for a perpetual licence with 12 months of updates and support. Row grouping, aggregation, pivoting and Excel export need the Premium plan, at $599 per developer per year or $1,318 per developer perpetual."
        },
        {
            "question": "What is a Data Grid in MUI?",
            "answer": "MUI X Data Grid is a React data grid component from MUI, the company behind Material UI. It is built for React only, needs Material UI as a peer dependency, and comes in Community, Pro, Premium and Enterprise plans."
        },
        {
            "question": "Which React data grid is free?",
            "answer": "AG Grid Community and the Community version of MUI X Data Grid are both free under the MIT licence. AG Grid Community includes row virtualisation, column pinning and lazy loading from the server. In the free MUI X Data Grid, row virtualisation is limited to 100 rows, and column pinning and server-side lazy loading need the Pro plan."
        },
        {
            "question": "Does MUI X Data Grid work with Angular or Vue?",
            "answer": "No. MUI X Data Grid is built for React only. AG Grid supports React, Angular, Vue and plain JavaScript. See [Getting Started](./getting-started/)."
        },
        {
            "question": "Can I use AG Grid for free?",
            "answer": "Yes. AG Grid Community is free and open source under the MIT licence, including for commercial use. AG Grid Enterprise is a paid licence that adds features such as row grouping, pivoting, Excel export and the Server-Side Row Model. See [Community vs Enterprise](./community-vs-enterprise/)."
        },
        {
            "question": "How much does an AG Grid licence cost?",
            "answer": "AG Grid Community is free. AG Grid Enterprise, and the Enterprise Bundle with AG Charts Enterprise, are perpetual licences priced per developer, with one year of updates and support. [Configure your licence](/license-pricing/) to see your price."
        }
    ],
